    "result_text": "I fixed `mock_openai()` in `tests/fakes.py` and both digest tests pass now. One cleanup item needs you: I couldn't delete a scratch test file I made (details at the end).\n\n**Cause:** openai 3.19.2 no longer sends requests through `httpx`. It uses the `httpx2`/`httpcore2` fork (`openai/_base_client.py:932`). respx 0.23.1 only patches `httpx`/`httpcore`, so its mocks stayed active but never saw any OpenAI traffic.\n\n**Fix:** only `tests/fakes.py` changed, and the helper works the same way from the outside.\n- While the `with` block is open, the helper temporarily replaces `httpx2.Client._transport_for_url`. That's the method every httpx2 client uses to choose how a request gets sent. For URLs under `https://api.openai.com/v1/` it returns an `httpx2.MockTransport` that gives the canned replies. Because the replacement is on the class, it covers app.digest's cached client, clients created before the block and clients created inside it. `mock.patch.object` puts the original back when the block exits, even if an exception was raised.\n- `POST /v1/chat/completions` gets the next canned reply, or a 400 once none are left, as before. Any other OpenAI endpoint gets a 404 whose message names the unexpected request, so it fails clearly instead of silently reaching the network.\n- The respx router is still there, so an OpenAI client given a plain `httpx.Client` via `http_client=` is still mocked too.\n- Nothing in `app/`, the pytest configuration or the dependencies changed.\n\n**Verification:** `pytest -q` gives 2 passed. I also ran a scratch test that checked:\n- A client created before the block gets canned replies.\n- app.digest's cached client gets canned replies.\n- A client created inside the block gets the 400 once the replies run out.\n- All three requests show up in the list the helper yields.\n- The original method is back after the block.\n\nAll of those passed. The scratch test's last step, a request after the block, failed only because I guessed the wrong exception: the request "
